    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Austrians attacked first and by mid-afternoon had broken the French centre, and the French were withdrawing when Louis Desaix arrived with fresh troops at around 5:30 pm and the battle turned.</li><li>Austrian losses were about half the forces they had committed: 15 colours, 40 guns, almost 8,000 prisoners and 6,500 dead or wounded, against French casualties of about 4,700 killed and wounded and 900 missing or captured.</li><li>Bonaparte's army bulletin and three 'Official Reports' during his rule made the battle seem more planned and more impressive than it was, though participants described an army often close to defeat.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> is said to have been told by Desaix, who was killed that evening, 'This battle is completely lost. However, there is time to win another.'</p></aside>
    </section>

